From 26bfde58788097ad8986058e50ed87217ebf0fa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:14:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] bitproxy: recover from sing-box hangs after long
 outages

Seen on a OnePlus 15: OxygenOS switched Wi-Fi off at night with mobile
data off (80 min without any network). When Wi-Fi came back the VPN
still looked on but passed no traffic, and Stop then hung forever
(sing-box's close never returned), so the app had to be force-stopped.
Not reproducible on the emulator (3 and 10 min outages, also in Doze,
recover), so guard against it instead:

- After the underlying network was gone for 2+ min and comes back,
  build a fresh sing-box instance (libbox reload). If that doesn't
  return within 20 s, end the process and have an alarm start the VPN
  service again 3 s later (Always-on does not restart it after process
  death: tested, still down after 2 min).
- Stop watchdog: if stopping hasn't finished within 15 s, end the
  process and show a notification instead of hanging on 'stopping'.
- EventLog: small on-disk log of start/stop/network lost and back/
  Apply/watchdog actions, shown in Diagnostics and included in the
  export, so the next incident leaves evidence (logcat on OxygenOS only
  covers ~90 s).

Upstream hooks: onFullyStopped() in the two places BoxService marks
itself Stopped.
